# TRUSTED PROGRAMS — the enforcement boundary, stated explicitly.
#
# Every artifact declaring evidence_source: program names the binary that
# produced it and that binary's hash. Without this file that claim is
# self-referential: a modified emitter records its own modified hash and
# every downstream check still passes.
#
# This file is the root of trust. It is NOT verified by anything in this
# toolchain. It must be pinned out of band — reviewed, signed, or committed
# and diffed — exactly as SLSA's trust in a build platform must be.
# Everything else here reduces to trusting these hashes.
#
# Names may be given bare (sk_emit.py) or as subcommands (sk_emit.route);
# sk-verify falls back from the full name to the base program.

